Naming: every surface type uses the collision-free `PhotoGallery*` prefix (verified: no other
`PhotoGallery*` definition exists in the Apple target). The sibling VehiclePhotoUpload owns the
`VehiclePhoto*` namespace; this surface does not redefine any of it.

Parity: the web source is a display-only wrapper around the shared `<Lightbox>` that renders a
square thumbnail grid (2/3/4 responsive) or an empty card and opens the lightbox at the tapped
index. Native reproduces the data shape, the composition (grid + empty card + open-at-index), and
ALL 5 extracted i18n keys verbatim:
   vehicles.photos.empty / vehicles.photos.emptyHelp / vehicles.photos.galleryNamed /
   vehicles.photos.gallery / vehicles.photos.openAt
The web `useTranslation` is bound through the P1/S10 facade. The deep zoom/pan/focus-trap of the
web `<Lightbox>` belongs to the shared lightbox atom (P4 component-library bundle); this surface
composes the existing shared `tsLightbox` presentation (apps/apple/Sources/Components/UI/
Overlays.swift) with the gallery-owned navigation (prev/next/counter/caption/swipe), exactly as
the web gallery delegates the immersive chrome to `<Lightbox>`. Every state from the web source
(empty / data) plus the P4 leaf contract (loading / error / stale / offline + the cached-grid
inline error on a failed reload) renders real chrome — no hidden surface. view.opened (P1/S11) is
emitted once on appear with slug "VehiclePhotoGallery".

